SSL scientific notation needs a digit, a decimal point, then the
exponent (diag.scientific_notation, error, on the number token, message
shows the corrected literal): 7e2, 9E+1 (sign kept in the suggestion) and
.5e1 all fire.
Suspected issue: #328 — under strict, undeclared_variable also reports the exponent fragments e2, E and e1 as variables; they are part of the malformed literal scientific_notation already reports (one typo, two findings).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Scale;
	:DECLARE nA, nB, nC;
	nA := 7e2;
	nB := 9E+1;
	nC := .5e1;
	:RETURN nA + nB + nC;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Scale;
	:DECLARE nA, nB, nC;
	nA := 7e2;
	nB := 9E + 1;
	nC := .5e1;
	:RETURN nA + nB + nC;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:8-3:9 error scientific_notation: SSL scientific notation requires a decimal point: use '7.0e2' instead of '7e2'
4:8-4:9 error scientific_notation: SSL scientific notation requires a decimal point: use '9.0E+1' instead of '9E+...'
5:8-5:10 error scientific_notation: SSL scientific notation requires a digit before the decimal point: use '0.5e1' instead of '.5e1'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
3:8-3:9 error scientific_notation: SSL scientific notation requires a decimal point: use '7.0e2' instead of '7e2'
3:9-3:11 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'e2' is not declared
4:8-4:9 error scientific_notation: SSL scientific notation requires a decimal point: use '9.0E+1' instead of '9E+...'
4:9-4:10 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'E' is not declared
5:8-5:10 error scientific_notation: SSL scientific notation requires a digit before the decimal point: use '0.5e1' instead of '.5e1'
5:10-5:12 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'e1' is not declared
